# mm.shell.board

The interactive board shell apps/mcu-shell runs: the console attached to the
selected mm.stdio driver, the level-2 command pack and the blink and sample
scripts installed, every buffer owned as one static block, and the event loop
that feeds console bytes to a Session and steps it. An application passes
Extras to add command packs, capabilities, and mounts before the session
begins, which is how apps/mcu-shell adds the file commands and its storage,
and apps/mcu-shell-sd its SD card too.
